1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:09,900
In the 1950s, four sisters in central Mexico ran some of the most feared brothels in the country. People called them Las Poquianchis.

2
00:00:09,920 --> 00:00:16,980
Their trap was simple: a newspaper ad. Housemaid wanted. Poor young women answered it… and never came home.

3
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:24,320
Inside, they were locked in, forced to work, and beaten. Those who got sick, or became inconvenient, disappeared.

4
00:00:24,340 --> 00:00:31,720
In 1964, a young woman named Catalina Ortega escaped and reached the police in León.

5
00:00:31,740 --> 00:00:37,740
Officers went to the sisters' ranch near San Francisco del Rincón… and started digging.

6
00:00:37,760 --> 00:00:45,980
Reports claimed ninety-one bodies: women, men, even unborn children. Historians still argue over the true number.

7
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:50,430
The surviving sisters were each sentenced to forty years in prison.

8
00:00:50,450 --> 00:00:58,934
For more than a decade, everyone knew what those houses were. Nobody asked where the girls went. This is Plot Twist with A&R.

